; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR LUNAR LANDER  -  land gently on the pad   (loads at $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; Load, cold-boot, press a key. Gravity pulls the lander down; the up arrow fires
; the main engine, <- and -> the side thrusters - one burst per press (hold a key
; to repeat), each costing fuel. Land with all three columns on the '=' pad,
; falling slowly and hardly drifting. ESC quits; any key flies again.
;
; VT100: cursor addressing, erase to end of line, hide/show cursor. No scrolling.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/lander_verify.py, V0061.34): an autopilot that reads the lander's registers and presses the arrow keys: it LANDS on three different moons (touchdown vy 5-8, vx -1..1, fuel left printed correctly); the ground drawn is exactly the height/pad tables and the pad is 7 level columns; every frame the lander is drawn whole in its cell with no copy left behind; lined up over the pad with the engine off from 12 rows it crashes ON the pad at vy 46; hands off it crashes where it comes down; an arrow key flies again; a lone ESC quits cleanly; a rerun without reloading lands again. ~5 frames a second; the moon takes ~6 s to draw.
; NOT YET RUN ON HARDWARE.
;
; 425 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A
; D 4005 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    RB = 0: the index for patching strings
; D 4009 11 0E 06 94    LOADXI R14 0694
; D 400D C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; SEED:
; D 400F C3             RAND                               Spin the generator until a key comes: every moon differs
; D 4010 CC             SERST
; D 4011 A1 00 0F       IFFALSEI SEED
; D 4014 BD 04 67       CALL ANYKEY                        Take it (an ESC on its own quits)
; NEW:
; D 4017 11 0E 06 85    LOADXI R14 0685
; D 401B C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       Clear, hide the cursor
; D 401D 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000
; D 4021 11 07 00 15    LOADXI R7 0015                     the ground starts at row 21
; HG:
; D 4025 C3             RAND                               one step of the random walk per column
; D 4026 21 09          COPYAX Acc -> R9
; D 4028 11 0A 00 03    LOADXI R10 0003
; D 402C 4D 9A          DIVXY R9 / R10
; D 402E 27             COPYREMA
; D 402F 21 09          COPYAX Acc -> R9                   0 up, 1 level, 2 down
; D 4031 50 79 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R9 -> R7
; D 4034 53 07 00 01    SUBXI R7 0001
; D 4038 86 07 00 11    TESTXI R7 0011
; D 403C A1 00 43       IFFALSEI H1
; D 403F 11 07 00 12    LOADXI R7 0012
; H1:
; D 4043 86 07 00 18    TESTXI R7 0018
; D 4047 A1 00 4E       IFFALSEI H2
; D 404A 11 07 00 17    LOADXI R7 0017
; H2:
; D 404E 22 07          COPYXA R7 -> Acc
; D 4050 2F 06 0D 00    WRITEIDX R6 0D00                   H[c]
; D 4054 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 4057 2F 06 0D 60    WRITEIDX R6 0D60                   P[c] = 0
; D 405B 42 06          INCX R6
; D 405D 86 06 00 51    TESTXI R6 0051
; D 4061 A1 00 25       IFFALSEI HG
; D 4064 C3             RAND                               where the pad goes
; D 4065 21 09          COPYAX Acc -> R9
; D 4067 11 0A 00 47    LOADXI R10 0047
; D 406B 4D 9A          DIVXY R9 / R10
; D 406D 27             COPYREMA
; D 406E 4E 00 01       ADDAI 0001
; D 4071 21 06          COPYAX Acc -> R6                   R6 = the pad's first column
; D 4073 2E 06 0D 00    READIDX R6 0D00
; D 4077 21 07          COPYAX Acc -> R7                   its height
; D 4079 11 09 00 07    LOADXI R9 0007
; PD:
; D 407D 22 07          COPYXA R7 -> Acc
; D 407F 2F 06 0D 00    WRITEIDX R6 0D00
